  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Import vanilla beans, retail &amp; wholesale Madagascar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DGGF pre-financing for the direct import of vanilla beans from Madagascar. Most of the vanilla is used for fulfilling a contract with a retailer. The remaining part is sold in bulk to regular customers in NL and DU, namely a wholesaler and two distilleries. After completion of the project, Matrada expects an extension of the contract with the buyers. Depending on the quantities, possibilities for new (partial) financing will be explored in 2026. Madagascar is one of the poorest countries in the world with few employment opportunities. By purchasing the vanilla at a premium from a locally rooted company, Matrada stimulates local employment. The 500 employees are dedicated to the production of vanilla pods, i.e. the time-consuming and complicated process of drying the green vanilla bean into a vanilla pod for the consumer. The supplier is FairTrade (Flo Cert), Bio (EkoCert &amp; SKAL) and Rain Forest Alliance certified and also supports vanilla farmers in the SAVA region through training and information.</narrative>
  </description>
